<mxCell id="note" value="A run that crashes, or ends without a valid outcome, is logged stopped by the wrapper itself, and so is one a check after it finds broken, with no after-hook run." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#4a4f6a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="856" width="1144" height="18" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note2" value="A failing before-hook prevents nothing, its failure in the run&amp;#x27;s inputs; a failing after-hook resumes the session once, then the run ends as a question. An answer resumes the waiting run named by its seq." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#4a4f6a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="874" width="1438" height="18" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
